text:
Your image is written in my soul,

and all I wish to write about you;

you alone wrote it, I read it

so inwardly that even from you I keep it hidden.


In this I am, and always will remain,

for though all I see in you cannot fit within me,

I believe in so much goodness that I cannot understand,

taking faith already as my premise.


I was born for nothing but to love you;

my soul has been cut to your measure:

by the soul's own nature, I love you.


I confess that I owe you all I have;

for you I was born, for you I have life,

for you I must die, and for you I die.
